A split of order `δ = p/e` in lowest terms produces a `μ_e`-orbit of nonzero `π`-roots of size `e`. That orbit cannot sit in `deg p = u_s` if `e > u_s`, so `den(δ) = e ≤ u_s`. The bound is `≤`, not “divides”: `δ = 5/2` has `e = 2`, `u_s = 3`, and Galois-stable `p = π(π² − c)`. Strengthening N5 to `e | u_s` would be false and would kill a surviving branch.

Sub-clusters keep the bound: a child packet of multiplicity `mm` has `den ≤ mm ≤ u_s`. The extra hypothesis Xu does not print is the `μ_e` action itself (Moh p.201 writes the same automorphism for major discs; Xu p.1 gives characteristic 0). The `(99,66)` skeleton satisfies §7.3.

